message: >-
  If you use the research findings, please cite this feasibility report rather
  than describing it as a released Qwen MoE model.
title: 'SixFinger Qwen3.8-27B Dense-to-MoE Feasibility Study'
type: software
authors:
  - name: SixFingerDev
date-released: '2026-11-04'
version: '1.0.0'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sixfingerdev/qwen38-dense-to-moe-feasibility'
abstract: >-
  Training-free first-layer Qwen3.8-27B SwiGLU sparsification investigation
  with held-out local-output error measurements, prototype code, and a
  documented negative result for near-lossless accelerated MoE deployment.
